36.921875 \nQ 37.984375 42.484375 42.96875 42.484375 \nQ 46.296875 42.484375 48.640625 40.53125 \nQ 49.421875 38.96875 49.421875 37.984375 \nQ 49.421875 36.53125 48.390625 35.5 \nQ 47.359375 34.46875 46.296875 34.46875 \nQ 45.015625 34.46875 43.40625 35.984375 \nQ 41.796875 37.5 40.4375 37.5 \nQ 39.265625 37.5 37.796875 34.96875 \nL 30.46875 22.46875 \nL 34.671875 8.6875 \nQ 35.640625 5.375 37.3125 5.375 \nQ 38.765625 5.375 40.421875 6.890625 \nQ 42.09375 8.40625 42.78125 9.671875 \nQ 43.171875 9.671875 43.75 8.890625 \nQ 44.34375 8.109375 44.34375 7.71875 \nQ 44.046875 6.0625 40.71875 2.78125 \nQ 37.40625 -0.484375 34.375 -0.484375 \nQ 30.28125 -0.484375 27.734375 8.015625 \nL 25.484375 15.625 \nL 19.34375 4.984375 \nQ 16.109375 -0.59375 11.140625 -0.59375 \nQ 7.8125 -0.59375 5.46875 1.375 \nQ 4.6875 2.734375 4.6875 3.90625 \nQ 4.6875 5.375 5.703125 6.390625 \nQ 6.734375 7.421875 7.8125 7.421875 \nQ 9.078125 7.421875 10.6875 5.90625 \nQ 12.3125 4.390625 13.671875 4.390625 \nQ 14.84375 4.390625 16.3125 6.9375 \nL 24.03125 20.21875 \nL 20.015625 33.296875 \nQ 19.046875 36.625 17.390625 36.625 \nQ 15.921875 36.625 14.25 35.109375 \nQ 12.59375 33.59375 11.921875 32.328125 \nQ 11.53125 32.328125 10.9375 33.109375 \nQ 10.359375 33.890625 10.359375 34.28125 \nQ 10.640625 35.9375 13.953125 39.203125 \nQ 17.28125 42.484375 20.3125 42.484375 \nz\n\" id=\"CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></path>\n     </defs>\n     <g transform=\"translate(252.62804 226.936045)scale(0.15 -0.15)\">\n      <use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></use>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p82df5710b8)\" d=\"M 91.835366 254.479379 \nL 217.145294 35.187005 \nL 217.145294 35.187005 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p82df5710b8)\" d=\"M 69.548701 37.675159 \nL 72.492222 64.095774 \nL 75.435744 88.493086 \nL 78.379266 110.867096 \nL 80.902285 128.434436 \nL 83.425303 144.515267 \nL 85.948322 159.10959 \nL 88.050838 170.135999 \nL 90.153353 180.130111 \nL 92.255869 189.091926 \nL 94.358384 197.021443 \nL 96.040397 202.621803 \nL 97.722409 207.561493 \nL 99.404422 211.840512 \nL 101.086434 215.458861 \nL 102.347943 217.739058 \nL 103.609453 219.647628 \nL 104.870962 221.184572 \nL 106.132472 222.349888 \nL 107.393981 223.143577 \nL 108.234987 223.466243 \nL 109.075993 223.623742 \nL 109.917 223.616074 \nL 110.758006 223.443238 \nL 111.599012 223.105234 \nL 112.860521 222.28854 \nL 114.122031 221.100218 \nL 115.38354 219.54027 \nL 116.645049 217.608694 \nL 117.906559 215.305491 \nL 119.588571 211.656468 \nL 121.270584 207.346775 \nL 122.952596 202.376411 \nL 124.634609 196.745377 \nL 126.737124 188.777517 \nL 128.83964 179.77736 \nL 130.942155 169.744906 \nL 133.044671 158.680154 \nL 135.56769 144.03982 \nL 138.090708 127.912978 \nL 140.613727 110.299628 \nL 143.136746 91.19977 \nL 146.080267 67.037821 \nL 149.023789 40.852569 \nL 149.444292 36.946652 \nL 149.444292 36.946652 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p82df5710b8\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"254.472611\" x=\"13.208695\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for Answer Choice D\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>For the line in the system:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The line slants sharply up from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 1.7)</li>\n<li>(1 comma 2.7)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For the parabola in the system:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The parabola opens upward.</li>\n<li>The vertex is at point (negative 1.7 comma 0).</li>\n<li>The parabola passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(negative 2.7 comma 1)</li>\n<li>(negative 1.7 comma 0)</li>\n<li>(negative 0.7 comma 1)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["06dc8a58-e2ed-42e7-8a32-1898779238a9"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The graph of a quadratic equation in the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals x squared plus c"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math> has its vertex at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma c right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. The first equation in the given system of equations is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals x squared plus 1.7"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1.7</mn></math>, so the graph of this quadratic equation has its vertex at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 1.7 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. The graph of a linear equation of the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals b minus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math> has a slope of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 1"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and a <em>y</em>-intercept at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma b right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. The second equation in the given system of equations is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 1.7 minus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, so the graph of this linear equation has a slope of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 1"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and a <em>y</em>-intercept at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 1.7 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Of the choices, only choice A has the graph of a quadratic equation with its vertex at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 1.7 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and the graph of a linear equation with a slope of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 1"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and a <em>y</em>-intercept at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 1.7 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This graph represents a system in which the second equation is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 1.7 plus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 1.7 minus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This graph represents a system in which the first equation is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals left parenthesis x plus 1.7 right parenthesis squared"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1.7</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals x squared plus 1.7"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1.7</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This graph represents a system in which the first equation is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals left parenthesis x plus 1.7 right parenthesis squared"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1.7</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals x squared plus 1.7"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1.7</mn></math>, and the second equation is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 1.7 plus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 1.7 minus x"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"75a32330","external_id":"3fb87a51-838d-423b-8abf-0dca2a3cf712","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"51b06885-6221-4570-9cfa-a3e385c7615f","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals x squared plus 1.7\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1.7</mn></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 1.7 minus x\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which graph represents the given system of equations?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"06dc8a58-e2ed-42e7-8a32-1898779238a9","content":"<p><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:x