</math> is a common factor of each term in the given expression, the given expression can be rewritten as <math alttext="x left parenthesis 23 x squared plus 2 x plus 9 right parenthesis"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>23</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext="23 x cubed plus 46 x squared plus 207 x"><mn>23</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>46</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>207</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext="207 x Superscript 4 plus 18 x cubed plus 9 x"><mn>207</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext="34 x cubed plus 34 x squared plus 34 x"><mn>34</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>34</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>34</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"772de699","external_id":"a7c54228-4ce0-4f08-8ae4-811ea92339af","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"4a4f0820-66c3-4252-a5ac-eaca79a59fd6","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"23 x cubed plus 2 x squared plus 9 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>23</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"7fdeed66-22ba-4edf-8538-2f3283228204","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"23 x left parenthesis x squared plus 2 x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"cc9763b9-041c-4653-b412-e07bba59b2f9","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"9 x left parenthesis 23 x cubed plus 2 x squared plus 1 right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"7b11260b-c1d7-463f-80b1-d0b9fdf6538f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x left parenthesis 23 x squared plus 2 x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"f825ddca-6cff-4504-ba19-b2b956dfcceb","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"34 left parenthesis x cubed plus x squared plus x right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}],"keys":["7b11260b-c1d7-463f-80b1-d0b9fdf6538f"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. Since <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is a common factor of each term in the given expression, the given expression can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"x left parenthesis 23 x squared plus 2 x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>23</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"23 x cubed plus 46 x squared plus 207 x\"><mn>23</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>46</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>207</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"207 x Superscript 4 plus 18 x cubed plus 9 x\"><mn>207</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"34 x cubed plus 34 x squared plus 34 x\"><mn>34</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>34</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>34</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554985,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"772de699","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1743430554985,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"a7c54228-4ce0-4f08-8ae4-811ea92339af","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"4a4f0820-66c3-4252-a5ac-eaca79a59fd6","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"23 x cubed plus 2 x squared plus 9 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>23</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["7b11260b-c1d7-463f-80b1-d0b9fdf6538f"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"7fdeed66-22ba-4edf-8538-2f3283228204","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"23 x left parenthesis x squared plus 2 x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"cc9763b9-041c-4653-b412-e07bba59b2f9","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"9 x left parenthesis 23 x cubed plus 2 x squared plus 1 right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"7b11260b-c1d7-463f-80b1-d0b9fdf6538f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x left parenthesis 23 x squared plus 2 x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"f825ddca-6cff-4504-ba19-b2b956dfcceb","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"34 left parenthesis x cubed plus x squared plus x right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. Since <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is a common factor of each term in the given expression, the given expression can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"x left parenthesis 23 x squared plus 2 x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>23</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"23 x cubed plus 46 x squared plus 207 x\"><mn>23</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>46</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>207</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"207 x Superscript 4 plus 18 x cubed plus 9 x\"><mn>207</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"34 x cubed plus 34 x squared plus 34 x\"><mn>34</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>34</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>34</mn><mi>x</mi></math>.</p>","externalid":"a7c54228-4ce0-4f08-8ae4-811ea92339af","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1743430554985,"updateDate":1743430554985}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554985, 1743430554985),
    ($SATQ$77c0cced$SATQ$, $SATQ$91e78971-fbd4-44f8-ad04-97fb96cf9931$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$e0288c07-4745-4626-ab5d-38dc79520715$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="y equals 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>2</mn>
			<msup>
				<mi>x</mi>
				<mn>2</mn>
			</msup>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>21</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>64</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="y equals 3 x plus a"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>3</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>a</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the given system of equations, <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> is a constant. The graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at exactly one point, <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4d742926-5ae4-4f3e-9944-9239f78ea2eb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 8\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"695984e6-3989-41bd-a993-4e2f4467df19","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"6188f848-7e39-4eea-8267-9791012b53f5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"bd269d7e-26db-4464-9088-a0c2d42bc593","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6188f848-7e39-4eea-8267-9791012b53f5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. It's given that the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at exactly one point, <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, in the <em>xy</em>-plane.&nbsp;Therefore, <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the only solution to the given system of equations. The given system of equations can be solved by subtracting the second equation, <math alttext="y equals 3 x plus a"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, from the first equation, <math alttext="y equals 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></math>. This yields <math alttext="y minus y equals left parenthesis 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64 right parenthesis minus left parenthesis 3 x plus a right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 64 minus a"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Since the given system has only one solution, this equation has only one solution. A quadratic equation in the form <math alttext="r x squared plus s x plus t equals 0"><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math>, and <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> are constants, has one solution if and only if the discriminant, <math alttext="s squared minus 4 r t"><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></math>, is equal to zero. Substituting <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="negative 24"><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></math> for <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math>, and <math alttext="negative a plus 64"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mi>a</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>64</mn>
</mrow>
</math> for <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> in the expression <math alttext="s squared minus 4 r t"><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></math> yields <math alttext="left parenthesis negative 24 right parenthesis squared minus left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis 64 minus a right parenthesis"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Setting this expression equal to zero yields <math alttext="left parenthesis negative 24 right parenthesis squared minus left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis 64 minus a right parenthesis equals 0"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, or <math alttext="8 a plus 64 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>a</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>64</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="64"><mn>64</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="8 a equals negative 64"><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>64</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="a equals negative 8"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext="negative 8"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math> for <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 64 minus a"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></math> yields <math alttext="0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 64 plus 8"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, or <math alttext="0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 72"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>72</mn></math>. Factoring <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> from the right-hand side of this equation yields <math alttext="0 equals 2 left parenthesis x squared minus 12 x plus 36 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="0 equals x squared minus 12 x plus 36"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis squared"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="0 equals x minus 6"><mrow>
	<mn>0</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>6</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> to both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="x equals 6"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math>, not <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"77c0cced","external_id":"91e78971-fbd4-44f8-ad04-97fb96cf9931","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"e0288c07-4745-4626-ab5d-38dc79520715","uId":"a5e69f0d-e3fd-4307-8261-7f31b6f986ed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t\t</msup>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>21</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>64</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 3 x plus a\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given system of equations, <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is a constant. The graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at exactly one point, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, in the <em>xy</em>-plane. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"4d742926-5ae4-4f3e-9944-9239f78ea2eb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 8\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"695984e6-3989-41bd-a993-4e2f4467df19","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"6188f848-7e39-4eea-8267-9791012b53f5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"bd269d7e-26db-4464-9088-a0c2d42bc593","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["6188f848-7e39-4eea-8267-9791012b53f5"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. It's given that the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at exactly one point, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, in the <em>xy</em>-plane.&nbsp;Therefore, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the only solution to the given system of equations. The given system of equations can be solved by subtracting the second equation, <math alttext=\"y equals 3 x plus a\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, from the first equation, <math alttext=\"y equals 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></math>. This yields <math alttext=\"y minus y equals left parenthesis 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64 right parenthesis minus left parenthesis 3 x plus a right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 64 minus a\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Since the given system has only one solution, this equation has only one solution. A quadratic equation in the form <math alttext=\"r x squared plus s x plus t equals 0\"><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> are constants, has one solution if and only if the discriminant, <math alttext=\"s squared minus 4 r t\"><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></math>, is equal to zero. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"negative 24\"><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"negative a plus 64\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>64</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> in the expression <math alttext=\"s squared minus 4 r t\"><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 24 right parenthesis squared minus left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis 64 minus a right parenthesis\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Setting this expression equal to zero yields <math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 24 right parenthesis squared minus left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis 64 minus a right parenthesis equals 0\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"8 a plus 64 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>64</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"64\"><mn>64</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"8 a equals negative 64\"><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>64</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"a equals negative 8\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"negative 8\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 64 minus a\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 64 plus 8\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 72\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>72</mn></math>. Factoring <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> from the right-hand side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals 2 left parenthesis x squared minus 12 x plus 36 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared minus 12 x plus 36\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis squared\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals x minus 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> to both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"x equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959824,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"77c0cced","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1691007959824,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":null,"external_id":"91e78971-fbd4-44f8-ad04-97fb96cf9931","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"a5e69f0d-e3fd-4307-8261-7f31b6f986ed","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["6188f848-7e39-4eea-8267-9791012b53f5"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. It's given that the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at exactly one point, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, in the <em>xy</em>-plane.&nbsp;Therefore, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the only solution to the given system of equations. The given system of equations can be solved by subtracting the second equation, <math alttext=\"y equals 3 x plus a\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, from the first equation, <math alttext=\"y equals 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></math>. This yields <math alttext=\"y minus y equals left parenthesis 2 x squared minus 21 x plus 64 right parenthesis minus left parenthesis 3 x plus a right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals 2 x squared minus 24 x plus 64 minus a\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Since the given system has only one solution, this equation has only one solution. A quadratic equation in the form <math alttext=\"r x squared plus s x plus t equals 0\"><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> are constants, has one solution if and only if the discriminant, <math alttext=\"s squared minus 4 r t\"><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></math>, is equal to zero. Substituting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"negative 24\"><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"negative a plus 64\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>64</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> in the expression <math alttext=\"s squared minus 4 r t\"><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 24 right parenthesis squared minus left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis 64 minus a right parenthesis\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Setting this expression equal to zero yields <math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 24 right parenthesis squared minus left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis 64 minus a right parenthesis equals 0\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"8 a plus 64 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>64</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"64\"><mn>64</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"8 a equals negative 64\"><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>64</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"a equals negative 8\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"negative 8\"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"