</math> for <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="h equals minus a left parenthesis t minus b right parenthesis squared plus c"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math> yields <math alttext="h equals minus a left parenthesis t minus 1.8 right parenthesis squared plus 51.84"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>51.84</mn></math>. It's also given that this softball hits the ground at&nbsp;<math alttext="3.6"><mn>3.6</mn></math> seconds; therefore, <math alttext="h equals 0"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> when <math alttext="t equals 3.6"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.6</mn></math>. Substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
